{"name":"Sweetie Pie","hex":"#e1bbdb","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweetie pie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sweetheart; a beloved person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweetie_pie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Term of endearment","blocks":[{"text":"A term of endearment is a word or phrase used to address or describe a person, animal or inanimate object for which the speaker feels love or affection. Terms of endearment are used for a variety of reasons, such as parents addressing their children and lovers addressing each other."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Term_of_endearment"},{"title":"List of Tiny Toon Adventures characters","blocks":[{"text":"The characters in the American animated television series Tiny Toon Adventures and its reboot Tiny Toons Looniversity were created by animator Tom Ruegger. The series chronicles the adventures of Buster Bunny, Babs Bunny and their various friends in the fictional city of Acme Acres. Most of the characters are anthropomorphic animals and humans based on the Looney Tunes characters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c7/TinyToons_characters.png/330px-TinyToons_characters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Tiny_Toon_Adventures_characters"},{"title":"Sweetie Pie (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweetie Pie\" is a song written by Eddie Cochran, Jerry Capehart, and Johnny Russell and recorded by Eddie Cochran. It was recorded in 1957 and released posthumously as a single on Liberty F-55278 in August 1960. In the UK the single rose to number 38 on the charts. The U.S. release did not chart. The flip side, \"Lonely\", reached number 41 on the UK singles chart. Keld Heich has recorded the song in 2010."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/12/Sweetie_Pie_Eddie_Cochran_London_Records_45.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweetie_Pie_(song)"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Redressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_%28Museo_del_Prado%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A detail of a painting by Jan Brueghel the Elder (1568–1625) and Peter Paul Rubens (1577–1640) depicting several bird pies. Cooked birds were frequently placed by European royal cooks on top of a large pie to identify its contents.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedressed_birds_-_Jan_Brueghel_I_%26_Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Taste_(Museo_del_Prado)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Roberto_Bompiani_-_A_Roman_Feast_-_72.PA.4_-_J._Paul_Getty_Museum